    "status": "unreviewed",
    "reviewers": [],
    "lastReviewedAt": null,
    "nextReviewDue": null,
    "notes": "SEED PACK - NOT AUTHORITATIVE. Table structure follows the published bye-laws; the numbers are plausible drafting defaults entered by the Garh AI team from secondary summaries, not transcribed from the primary document. An empanelled local architect must replace every value, confirm every citation, and move the pack to 'reviewed' before it is used on a submission."
  },
  "disclaimer": "Advisory only, not an approval. Every value in this pack is marked 'seed': it was drafted by the Garh AI team from secondary summaries of the bye-laws and has NOT been verified against the primary document or by a local architect. Do not rely on it for a sanction submission. The architect of record remains responsible for compliance; verify each figure against the current bye-laws and any local amendment before signing a drawing.",
  "notes": "Setbacks are tabulated twice on purpose: once by plot area and once by access-road width. Both families are minima, so the larger requirement governs - that is how the bye-law's two-axis table behaves. FAR, height and floor limits are indexed on the access-road width, coverage on plot area. Karnataka also permits height as a function of (road width + front setback); that formula is NOT encoded here and must be added at review as a custom check if the reviewing architect wants it.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "label": "BBMP Building Bye-laws 2020",
      "publisher": "Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike",
      "year": 2020,
      "obtained": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Revised Master Plan 2015 - Zoning of Land Use and Regulations",
      "publisher": "Bangalore Development Authority",
      "year": 2007,
      "obtained": false
    },
    {
      "label": "BWSSB (Amendment) Regulations 2009 - rainwater harvesting",
      "publisher": "Bangalore Water Supply and Sewerage Board",
      "year": 2009,
      "obtained": false
    }
  ],
